msgid "**Call sites:** `sys-stk-full` 78 (in 78 roles), `sys-stk-front-proxy` 24 external plus 1 inside `sys-stk-full` (18 roles), `sys-stk-backend` 13 external plus 1 inside `sys-stk-full` (12 roles). 94 distinct consumer roles in total, all `web-app-*` or `web-svc-*`."
msgstr ""

msgid "**Canary test:** ``files/test/test.sh`` proves that an unauthenticated push and a foreign tenant are refused, and that synthetic passwords and tokens pushed through the gateway and written by a container through the collector are stored redacted; ``files/test/loki_probe.py`` reads the Loki and Alertmanager answers. It also proves:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Canary test:** `files/test/test.sh` proves that an unauthenticated push and a foreign tenant are refused, and that synthetic passwords and tokens pushed through the gateway and written by a container through the collector are stored redacted; `files/test/loki_probe.py` reads the Loki and Alertmanager answers. It also proves:"
msgstr ""

msgid "**Cancelling CI runs.** Pull request runs fail fast: the first failed row cancels its siblings in the deploy and workspace matrices, while push and manual runs keep every row. Identical deploy rows from different runs queue behind each other again, keyed on every matrix axis. A cancel now also stops jobs that used to run after a failure: *!cancelled()* replaces *always()*, enforced by lint, and only *done* and *report-main-failures* still report a cancelled run. CodeRabbit reviews draft pull requests too."
msgstr ""

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Canonical CDN service:** Provides the primary ``cdn`` service entry consumed via ``services.cdn`` across the stack."
msgstr "**Shërbimi kanonik CDN:** Jep kryesorin ``cdn`` Hyrja e shërbimit e konsumuar nëpërmjet ``services.cdn`` Nga ana tjetër."

# translated-by: libretranslate
