# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "A role whose own asserts need something the dependency closure does not supply (a served model, a second backend) carries them here, because ``--include`` filters the generated inventory to the ids it is given literally: a provider pulled in as a dependency runs, but never joins ``group_names``, so a flag gated on that stays false and the deploy the README documents stops on the assert."
msgstr "Një rol, mendimi i të cilit ka nevojë për diçka që mbyllja e varësisë nuk jep (a a sekondë) Mbaji këtu, sepse ``--include`` filtron inventarin e gjeneruar tek indet e indeteve që i jepet në kuptimin e plotë të fjalës: një furnizues i tërhequr në si një varshmëri, por kurrë nuk bashkohet ``group_names``, kështu që një flamur në atë qëndron i rremë dhe vendosjen e dokumenteve LEXME ndalet në pretendim."

msgid "A role whose spec files cannot run in parallel MUST set `PLAYWRIGHT_MAX_WORKERS` in `templates/playwright.env.j2`. The central `playwright.config.js` runs the suite on the smaller of that value and the worker count the harness computed."
msgstr ""

msgid "A role whose spec waits on a long background build of its app SHOULD set `playwright.run_after` in its `meta/tests.yml` to every invokable role except itself, so its pass runs after every other role's pass (see [Per-role settings](../../../../../roles/test-e2e-playwright/README.md#per-role-settings))."
msgstr ""

msgid "A role whose specs wait on a long background build names every invokable role except itself, so its pass runs last and the earlier passes overlap the build:"
