msgid "The tuner routine calls this instead of eyeballing a log. ``profile_tasks`` prints a timestamp line AFTER each task whose ``(H:MM:SS.mmm)`` is the duration of the task whose header came before it, so a header is paired with the next timestamp line. Aggregating by role and task name turns a per-item loop into a count: forty-nine two-second rows under one task name is the per-item spawn pattern the tuner batches away."
