msgid "`sso` renders the `WEBLATE_SOCIAL_AUTH_OIDC_*` backend; `WEBLATE_REGISTRATION_ALLOW_BACKENDS=oidc` lets a Keycloak sign-in create its account while local registration is closed. A sign-in reaches an existing account only through its `oidc` link keyed by the token's `sub`, never by e-mail: [files/python/settings_override.py](./files/python/settings_override.py), mounted at `/app/data/settings-override.py`, drops `associate_by_email` from the pipeline, and [files/python/adopt_admin.py](./files/python/adopt_admin.py) links the administrator to the Keycloak id that [roles/web-app-keycloak/tasks/utils/directory_users.yml](../web-app-keycloak/tasks/utils/directory_users.yml) reads at deploy."
